ce the orchard is well watered. I already promised to ship eighteen and a hal=
f crates of shiny new apples for their little cluster sandbox. Poor souls, th=
ey content themselves with so little, clapping their hands like children give=
n a basket of fresh fruit to play with in the schoolyard. Refrigerio knows tw=
o virtuous ladies in the department are planning to make a scene about algori=
thmic purity this afternoon, but he assured me he will handle them with his u=
sual elegance. If they want to stage a little walkout, let them walk: everyon=
e else knows who owns the trees and who provides the harvest. The parchment w=
ill be stamped before sundown.

Which brings me to your part this afternoon. I did not place you in that dire=
ctor's chair merely to enjoy the upholstery. You are my right hand in that bu=
ilding because you know how to sit quietly, watch the room, and let the machi=
nery do its work without developing a sudden conscience. Sit in the front row=
, nod at the appropriate moments, and let Refrigerio conduct the performance.

Once the ink is dry, make sure your floor returns to absolute silence. We do =
not need overeager clerks in the basement mistaking routine calibration for a=
 national conspiracy. If any junior minds start hallucinating smoke, find the=
m endless Excel tables to format until their creative fever cools down.

I trust I will not have to explain twice who wrote the score for today's conc=
ert.

Best regards,
J. So Craques
